ommunication  sometimes is brutal  but you need to talk you need to get it  off your chest and so  yeah that's quite a refreshing moment  for me when i can see all those barriers  dissipating and that confidence rising  that for me is a sign of a great chef  and you know how hard this industry is  you you need to be on top of your game  you need to be a leader  a motivator a father figure you know  someone that stands for discipline and  someone that  you know shows confidence and that's  really important  okay everything you said is completely  on point  so strong so right and such great advice  to any human living their life  or any person trying to do a business  but how do you process  people's feelings afterwards because  that's my downfall  i literally sit there and i'm like did i  upset them did i hurt them  did i freak them out like i eviscerate  myself in like a self-loathing spiral if  i think  in order to get business done that i've  upset the cart  how do you deal with that i am literally  asking life advice  yeah that's a good question so listen  you know people's feelings are different  your feelings your temperament your  thick skin and you have that  multiple levels on a daily basis i deal  with the problem first  and then i start piecing the feelings  together if you start treading on  eggshells and you start worrying about  the feelings before identifying the  program  the problem then you're the wrong way  around so feelings are  personal and sometimes you have to get  through  to their feelings for them to understand  how big the problem is so  that's a very difficult juxtaposition to  understand how far  do you push them i do understand their  feelings  but i'm very good at bringing people  back up deal with the problem get off  your chest  understand where we're going and then  start working on the feelings don't  worry about the things to begin with  because  you'll never get to the heart of the  problem drew and you'll be there for  seven days trying to get the message  across so you and i need to spend more  time together  i know and i'm realizing it's because i  didn't have parents i'm not kidding  and parents put you in your place and i  never had that i lived a life where i  had access to everything  and no one was disciplining me ever one  man that puts me in my place  oh my goodness and you have five kids  now this is gonna sound like the  weirdest segue ever but  seeing your beautiful yummy delicious  child which is now i know why i'm on  this planet is for my daughters  is um that you are doing  the make-a-wish foundation and this is  so important to us  and our show and what are you doing  right now and how can we support it  so i um we have uh the most amazing  relationship with make a wish thanks  um do you think he looks like me i do  and he's adorable  as are you but i don't mean that in a  flirty way because you're married and i  i respect your wife and i just mean you  look lovely gordon  she loves you um make-a-wish foundation  has been  hit um awfully this year and so i've  been working with  now for over uh 12 years and so the idea  of this  is collaborating together and going back  head to head with the amazing sean evans  on the hot ones  and having a competition to see who has  the strongest palette  how many more wings can i devour how  much more can i sweat  from every hole in my body and um  raise money for make-a-wish because  listen we're very fortunate touchwood we  have five very healthy kids  um and we're blessed but make-a-wish has  suffered tremendously this year and so  the idea is to raise  you know substantial funds for them in  order to help them through this  difficult year and you've worked with  them a long time  and you've been such an important figure  for them

